// Stdin plugin — the dmenu replacement.
//
// Used by the helper scripts (clipboard-pick, window-switch, notif-history),
// which pipe a list in and read the chosen line back:
//
//   cliphist list | anyrun --plugins libstdin.so
//
// preserve_order is true so those lists keep the order the script produced —
// cliphist already returns newest first, and the notification history is
// deliberately newest-first. Sorting by fuzzy score would scramble both when
// the query is empty, which is the common case.
//
// max_entries is higher than the default 5 because the clipboard history is
// browsed by scrolling, not by typing.

Config(
    allow_invalid: false,
    max_entries: 12,
    preserve_order: true,
)
